{
  "summary": "VIP (CEO) Dana Whitfield, user_id 1. Got a new iPhone yesterday; Duo pushes no longer arrive, so she can't connect to VPN. She needs VPN for a board prep call at 2 PM ET today, so this is time-sensitive. Checks: account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked, vpn_access true. Duo enrolled 2025-12-13 with duo_push on 'Dana's phone', which is most likely still the old device. Sign-in logs (14 days): 9 successes, all from New York on residential/corporate networks at about 08:07 ET. No mfa_denied, no failed passwords, no hosting networks, so no signs of compromise or unrequested pushes. Laptop BL-LT-0101 is online, checked in today, no warnings. Still needed (KB-004 new-phone steps): verify her identity by calling back the number on file (not any number from the ticket), reactivate Duo Mobile on the new iPhone, then send a test push and confirm VPN works before 2 PM. Escalated because she is a VIP and the Duo device change needs identity verification, which Tier 1 tools can't do.",
  "reason": "KB-004 new-phone reactivation needs callback verification and Duo reactivation; VIP user with a deadline"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for letting us know. Your account looks fine. The pushes aren't coming through because Duo is still linked to your old phone. To move it to your new iPhone, a technician needs to call you at the number we have on file to confirm it's you. Then they'll set up Duo on the new phone with you and send a test push. I've passed this to our senior team as urgent and told them about your 2 PM call. Please keep your new iPhone nearby, and install the Duo Mobile app from the App Store if it isn't on there yet. That will speed things up.",
  "internal_note": "I checked the account: it's active, nothing is blocked, failed_login_count is 0, and vpn_access is true. Duo is enrolled (duo_push, set up 2025-12-13) on 'Dana's phone', which is most likely her old device. Her sign-in logs for the last 14 days show 9 successes, all from New York around 08:07 ET on residential or corporate networks. There are no MFA denials, no failed passwords and no hosting networks, so I saw no signs of compromise or KB-031 red flags. Her laptop BL-LT-0101 is online and healthy. Per the KB-004 new-phone steps, we need to verify her by calling the number on file, reactivate Duo Mobile on the new iPhone and send a test push. I escalated to Tier 2 (escalation 1) because she is a VIP/CEO, the Duo device change needs identity verification, and she needs VPN working before her 2 PM ET call. No action tools were queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-004",
    "KB-013"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
